Figure 2: Mammalian muscle spindle showing typical position in a muscle (left), neuronal connections in spinal cord (middle) and expanded schematic (right). The spindle is a stretch receptor with its own motor supply consisting of several intrafusal muscle fibres. The sensory endings of a primary (group Ia) afferent and a secondary (group II) afferent coil around the non-contractile central portions of the intrafusal fibres.}
\par \pard\plain \s42\rtlch\af9\afs21\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af4\loch\sl-270\slmult0\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa0\ltrpar\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f4\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe2052\qj\li0\lin0{\loch
rapidly adapting afferent activity, muscle force increases reflexively until the gripped object no longer moves. Such a rapid response to a tactile stimulus is a clear indication of the role played by somatosensory neurons in motor activity.}
\par \pard\plain \s42\rtlch\af9\afs21\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af4\loch\sl-270\slmult0\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa0\ltrpar\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f4\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe2052\qj\fi250\li0\lin0{\loch
The slowly adapting }{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\loch\i\loch
Merkel\u8217\'92s receptors}{\loch
 are responsible for form and texture perception. As would be expected for receptors mediating form perception, Merkel\u8217\'92s receptors are present at high density in the digits and around the mouth (50/mm\u178\'b2 of skin surface), at lower density in other glabrous surfaces, and at very low density in hairy skin. This innervations density shrinks progressively with the passage of time so that by the age of 50, the density in human digits is reduced to 10/mm\u178\'b2. Unlike rapidly adapting axons, slowly adapting fibers respond not only to the initial indentation of skin, but also to sustained indentation up to several seconds in duration.}
\par \pard\plain \s42\rtlch\af9\afs21\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af4\loch\sl-270\slmult0\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa0\ltrpar\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f4\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe2052\qj\fi250\li0\lin0{\loch
Activation of the rapidly adapting }{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\loch\i\loch
Pacinian corpuscles}{\loch
 gives a feeling of vibration, while the slowly adapting }{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\loch\i\loch
Ruffini corpuscles}{\loch
 respond to the lataral movement or stretching of skin.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af8\afs28 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\sl-300\slmult0\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar1\sb280\sa160\keepn\ltrpar\cf1\f6\fs28\dbch\af8\li0\lin0{\loch
